           Add the same amount (equal to the sample) of Benedict’s reagent/solution to the test tube;
           Half fill the beaker with water and heat it up over a Bunsen burner;
           Use a tong to put the test tube into the beaker of warm water/water-bath;
           Observe the colour of the solution in the test tube which changes according to the concentration of the
           reducing sugar in the feed;
           If the colour remains blue, no reducing sugar;
           Colour changes to green/yellow/orange/brick red (depending on the concentration);

